From 7959d2f730669a46024fb29f039047ea078b1e2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:31:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] reserve green sidebar card squares for worker waits

Green no longer conflates completed, unread work with waiting for an agent.
Use emerald for stalled agent-owned work and current validated queued-card
execution evidence; use violet for done, not yet seen. Keep completed-card
attention amber and preserve aggregate-only backend fallback behavior.
Deduplicate queued execution identities and reject expired/conflicting evidence
through the shared projector; cap queued refinement at the live card count.

Update accessible tooltips, i18n type/key registry/fallback gaps and consumer tests.

Proof:
- Updated colour tests fail on main (4 assertion failures).
- Queued run_id/generation regressions fail on main (2 assertion failures).
- Focused vitest: 392 passed across squares, row and projector suites.
- Renderer tsc --noEmit: passed.
- Applicable eslint and i18n key verification: passed.
- scripts/hermes-python scripts/check --base origin/main: 21 checks passed.
